WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.410
A relationship meltdown, a new tattoo, and
an ex hit with criminal charges.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:09.130
Here's what really happened to Brandi Passante
from Storage Wars.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.560
"Interesting is one way to put it."

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.410
Fame was a surprise to Brandi and Jarrod back
when "Storage Wars" debuted in 2010.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.410
They weren't expecting their appearances on
the show to go anywhere, but when they did,

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.010
Brandi and Jarrod weren't ready for any of
it.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:29.240
Brandi went from full-time mom and part-time
worker, to clocking 60 hours a week on the job.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.970
The commitment also made her miss out on important
family events, like her daughter's first day

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.500
of kindergarten.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.829
Because of that, she took a temporary leave
of absence from the show in 2014 — with

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:39.969
Jarrod in tow.

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:45.460
Suddenly spending every waking minute together
for the show, Brandi and Jarrod's personalities

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.239
started to collide like never before.

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:53.300
At the time, they were also co-managing their
Now and Then thrift store in Orange, California,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.800
which wasn't making anything easier.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.920
Brandi explained to the Times-Standard,

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:01.870
"Working together as a couple every day is
quite an obstacle to overcome.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:07.289
We're together 24 hours a day, seven days
a week trying to make business decisions together."

00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:08.770
"What was I thinking?"

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:13.190
As fans witnessed on the show, the pair were
often at each other's throats, but things

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.670
were apparently even worse offscreen.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.990
As Jarrod admitted to the OC Register,

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.170
"It makes our dysfunction seem a little less
dysfunctional."

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:26.390
Leveraging off their successful brand, the
couple soon landed their very own spin-off

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.039
show, "Brandi &amp; Jarrod: Married to the Job."

00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:33.609
The series followed the pair's journey as
business owners, partners, and parents.

00:01:33.609 --> 00:01:37.450
At one point, the couple even seemed to be
headed to the altar, but they never actually

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.619
ended up tying the knot.

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:42.369
"I mean, after fifteen years of being with
Jarrod, I mean, I just assumed that that ship

00:01:42.369 --> 00:01:43.369
had sailed."

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:48.899
Unfortunately for the duo, the show failed
to garner the same buzz that "Storage Wars" did.

00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:51.060
A&amp;E pulled the plug on the show after just
eight episodes.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:57.159
Brandi and Jarrod's relationship was over
long before they went public with it in 2021,

00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:00.909
but it was clear they were on thin ice back
in 2018.

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:05.180
Jarrod's absence from Brandi's Instagram was
obvious to eagle-eyed fans — as well as

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.360
the media.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.470
Some outlets even spotted the star without
her engagement ring, and cited a few photo

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.090
ops with new guys.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:16.420
Not to be left in the dust, Jarrod also went
public with girlfriend Rochel Beckman.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:21.160
Given the overwhelming evidence of trouble
between the two, no one was truly surprised

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.470
when Brandi finally broke the news that it
was over.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:29.310
Season 13 of "Storage Wars" brought about
one of the show's biggest switch-ups: the

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:33.350
couple formerly known as the Young Guns would
no longer be working as a team.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:38.000
If anyone thought that meant less drama, they
were wrong, as Jerrod didn't hesitate to make

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.000
things personal.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.930
"If Brandi bids on it, I'll probably bid."

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:46.211
During the run-up to the Season 13 premiere,
Brandi posted a promo shot on Twitter, in

00:02:46.211 --> 00:02:49.230
which Jarrod's face was fully covered with
a devil emoji.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.730
"I could watch this all day long."

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.520
For Brandi, the drama on the show was one
thing.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:00.950
In real life, however, when Jarrod showed
up at a gathering he wasn't invited to, things

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.920
got physical when he allegedly shoved Brandi
multiple times.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.590
Brandi would go on to claim that similar incidents
contributed to the end of their decades-long

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:09.820
relationship.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:14.530
In her efforts to move forward, she even got
a tattoo to symbolize her journey toward independence.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:19.230
Jarrod denied the allegations, but was charged
with domestic battery, according to TMZ.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:23.740
A&amp;E launched an investigation into the matter,
and while the findings were never revealed,

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:27.180
Jarrod was nowhere to be seen on the show's
14th season.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:31.560
The breakup left Brandi with deep psychological
wounds, and she had trouble cultivating her

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.990
own identity as a single woman.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:39.160
However, after nearly a decade spent living
as one half of a pair, Brandi is finally taking

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.160
control of her own destiny.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:46.190
The star addressed rumors about her relationship
status in February of 2021, and while she

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:49.690
admitted that she's dated a little, she's
currently thriving on her own.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:55.840
After the split, Brandi got primary custody
of the couple's two teens, Payton and Cameron.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.250
While raising them alone might seem like a
big task, the star has admitted that she had

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:03.980
been pretty much doing it herself even when
Jerrod was in the picture.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:08.050
As for how she's perfected her work-life balance,
she told MyLifetime.com,

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:12.220
"I used to be a stay-at-home mom and it was
very difficult for me.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:17.070
I love my kids, but I felt alienated and depressed
when I didn't have a career, so I think I'm

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.980
a better parent because I work.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:20.380
I'm happier because of it."

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:23.010
"My mom wants you to shut your face!"

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.330
"That's my son, Cameron."

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:28.480
Even though she's always glammed up for the
cameras herself, Brandi has dutifully protected

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.840
her kids' privacy.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:32.810
When they were younger, they were never seen
on social media.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:38.640
Now that they've grown up, Brandi is happy
to share the occasional peek into her family life.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:43.240
"Storage Wars" may have netted Brandi an estimated
$2 million fortune, but the reality star is

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.320
happy to give back to those in need.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:49.440
These days, she's advocating for women who
have also faced domestic violence.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:52.550
Brandi works closely with the Women's Own
Worth organization.

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:58.220
As the host of their annual WOWapalooza event
in 2019, she helped the charity bring in roughly

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.690
$100,000 in donations.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:04.870
Brandi finds her charity work extremely rewarding:
as she told The Saline Courier,

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:09.100
"I have experienced some things in my life,
and it's a really wonderful cause.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.580
[...] I wanted to help in any way possible."

